

A simple signal generator built using Arduino Nano that produces a **Triangle Wave signal**, with frequency controlled by a **potentiometer** — visualized live on the **Arduino IDE Serial Plotter**.


## Overview

This project demonstrates how Arduino can simulate a basic signal generator by sending structured values over Serial communication.
The potentiometer controls the signal frequency in real-time, and the output is plotted using Arduino IDE's built-in Serial Plotter — making it a great tool for understanding signal behavior without an oscilloscope.

## Concepts Covered

- Digital Signal Generation
- Potentiometer as Frequency Controller
- ADC (Analog to Digital Conversion)
- PWM Output (Pin D9)
- Serial Plotter Visualization
- Real-time Signal Monitoring


